{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Righteousness, righteousness.</b> He speaks with the litigants. The reason for two occurrences: to pursue justice whether he gains or loses by it, or one after another all your days, or for emphasis." "<b>That you may live.</b> He speaks with those who enter the land." "<b>And possess it.</b> He speaks with their children. The meaning is that this inheritance will endure for you. And the matter with which the judge must begin is concerning idol worship that is publicly known first, as in 'You shall not plant for yourself an Asherah,' for so is the law concerning an idolatrous city [עיר הנדחת] after one [witness] within."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Resolved עם בעלי הריב ידבר as 'He speaks with the litigants,' i.e., the subject is Moses addressing those who come to judgment.", 2 "The final clause ע״ג אחר אחת בתוך is textually difficult; possibly abbreviations for עיר הנדחת, עד אחד, עדים, or similar legal terms. Rendered hyper-literally; meaning uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:47.311150663Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}